      "source": "https://www.opendurham.org/category/neighborhood/rougemont",
      "category": "etymology",
      "quality": "good"
    },
    {
      "id": 2,
      "text": "The town’s old train depot is the last remaining depot in Durham County, and locals are working hard to preserve it.",
      "sourceSentenceIds": [
        1
      ],
      "sourceLabels": [
        "Web source 1"
      ],
      "source": "https://www.opendurham.org/category/neighborhood/rougemont",
      "category": "landmark",
      "quality": "good"
    },
    {
      "id": 3,
      "text": "The original Rougemont station burned in 1938 and was rebuilt in a similar style shortly after.",
      "sourceSentenceIds": [
        12
      ],
      "sourceLabels": [
        "Web source 1"
      ],
      "source": "https://www.opendurham.org/category/neighborhood/rougemont",
      "category": "history",
      "quality": "good"
    },
    {
      "id": 4,
      "text": "Rougemont sits 17 miles north of Durham’s center, making it a quiet northern suburb of the city.",
